    "description": "Partakes in the development of the Encounter Exchange project: A cloud-based, medical Picture Archiving System (PACS) for storing medical studies, a web application to manage and view patient records and studies, a WebGL-based viewer that allows real-time image manipulation of medical studies, and a RESTful web service back-end to provide a platform-independent API for a variety of client-applications.\n\nFollows the FDA approval process to release Encounter Exchange as a Class 2 medical device. Ensures that Encounter Exchange meets the HIPAA requirements for Protected Health Information.\n\nAutomates the project build process with ANT scripting for more rapid deployments.\n\nImproves SQL Server Database schema, stored procedures, and scripts to maximize performance, manageability, and ease of deployment.",
